# Adapt the decision brief into three presentation pages — learner brief

Fictional Northstar Services training material.

## Approved fictional facts
F1 September budget USD 200,000.
F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%.
F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel.
F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved.
F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.
## Supplied options
D1 maintain support one month, estimated incremental USD 8,000.
D2 reduce support, estimated two-week delay.
D3 controller recommends D1; CFO decision requested September 26. Neither option approved.
D4 revenue effect unknown. Estimates are fictional writing inputs.


## Task

The CFO will discuss the same decision in a short leadership meeting. Specify the message of each page.

## Actions


1. Assign one purpose to each page: situation, supplied options, decision.
2. Ask AI for three factual titles and brief speaker notes.
3. Check that titles do not imply revenue impact or approval that the packet does not establish.
4. Write a plain-text equivalent for the suggested comparison table.
5. Reconcile dates, amounts, and recommendation status across all pages.


## Output
Three page titles; key message per page; supporting facts; speaker notes; text equivalent of any suggested visual.
